Adds ILO_SPACE, the data type that syncs ilo's Spaces with their pinned tabs and folders, and lets
the core give its controller (//browser_core/hooks.h, set in //browser_core/sync_spaces.cc).

Only what makes the type exist is here: its enum value, its table entry, its field in
EntitySpecifics and the switches that list every type. Its message is one bytes field, holding
//browser_core's own message, so the Space's fields change without touching Chromium. The type is
always preferred, since the sidebar is the browser, and encrypted under the custom passphrase, as
every type ilo syncs is. Its field number is far above Google's, so none of theirs takes it, and
its enum value sits after BOOKMARKS rather than last, where Google adds each new type. Google's
metrics have no value for it, so it counts as kUnspecified there.

Google adds a type about once a milestone, and each new type changes the three counts here
(`64 + 1`): on a conflict, take Google's count and keep the `+ 1`.

